{"key":"enterprise/T1561","id":"T1561","name":"Disk Wipe","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["impact"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows","Network Devices"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may wipe or corrupt raw disk data on specific systems or in large numbers in a network to interrupt availability to system and network resources. With direct write access to a disk, adversaries may attempt to overwrite portions of disk data. Adversaries may opt to wipe arbitrary portions of disk data and/or wipe disk structures like the master boot record (MBR). A complete wipe of all disk sectors may be attempted. To maximize impact…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1561","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--1988cc35-ced8-4dad-b2d1-7628488fa967","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:27.697Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0054","name":"Drive Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0054","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--73ff2dcc-24b1-4368-b9dc-706dd9e68354","page":"telemetry/DC0054/"},{"id":"DC0046","name":"Drive Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0046","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--4dcd8ba3-2075-4f8b-941e-39884ffaac08","page":"telemetry/DC0046/"},{"id":"DC0079","name":"Driver Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0079","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3551476e-14f5-4e48-a518-e82135329e03","page":"telemetry/DC0079/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","pa